message: "If you use CircleFlow in teaching materials, slides or papers, please cite it as below."
title: "CircleFlow: Gas Flow in the Anesthesia Machine and Breathing Circuit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Asamoto
    given-names: Masaaki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0770-2860"
    affiliation: "Department of Anesthesiology, Graduate School of Medicine, The University of Tokyo"
version: "1.9.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24050136"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
url: "https://anesthesia-sims.github.io/circleflow/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/anesthesia-sims/circleflow"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A free, in-browser educational simulator that shows gas flow in the
  anesthesia machine and breathing circuit as moving particles. It covers
  bellows (ascending), piston, blower (turbine) and volume reflector
  ventilators in 17 scenarios, with Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese and
  Traditional Chinese (Taiwan) versions. Code is MIT-licensed; figures and text are CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - anesthesia
  - anesthesia machine
  - breathing circuit
  - circle system
  - ventilator
  - medical education
  - simulation
  - clinical engineering
